I don't know whether to think of this "best game so far" as cheating
though: I ended up using Explore mode for the first time this game,
after angering that stupid Minetown Priest.  Other than my first
encounter with a Giant Eel, and the Priestess of Moloch on the Valley
of the Dead, though, I was never in the remotest danger of death.

I was spoiled to the extent that I DL'd a solution to Sokoban, and
found the automated note-sorting thing for the Castle's drawbridge.
But other than that, I kept myself clean.

Next time I want to manage my stashes better so I don't end up running
through 20 dungeon levels hunting for particular items.

What's kinda funny about Nethack is that although it's a single-player
game, the Pet and your God both display (to me) unpredictable
behavior, and you have to manage your relationships with them pretty
carefully!  I made Set angry a couple of times, and have no clue why;
something to figure out later, I guess.






